==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Amazing combo potential.
* One of the best stun support fruits in the game for [[Swords]] and [[Guns]].
* Spectacular for grinding.
* Most moves [[Instinct/Break|break Instinct]].
* Some moves have low endlag.
* Overall very versatile.
* Very good against [[Magnet]] users

|{{Ability|TAP}}
* Can be held infinitely.
* Can hit multiple targets.
* Can be used very quickly as a tap up close to break [[Instinct]].

|{{Ability|Z}}
* Can be spammed.
* Possesses auto-aim when the user aims near an enemy, similar to [[Godhuman]]’s {{Ability|Godhuman|C}}.
* Good for disrupting combos.
* Z2 breaks instinct and pulls enemies toward the player.
* Z3 chains and damages nearby enemies, making it useful for grinding.

|{{Ability|X}}
* Large [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
* Extremely reliable stun, perfect set up for a [[Sword]] or [[Gun]] attack.
* Long stun (can be further increased by adding Z1 orbs to the cloud).
* Extremely good against enemies with large hitboxes.
* Extremely good for killing [[Sea Beast|Sea Beasts]] when used with the Z1 orbs.
*If used with Z3 with great aim and prediction, can hit midair opponents within its range.
* [[instinct/Break|Breaks Instinct]] on ground.
* Extended storm makes grinding very easy, even allowing the player to use any [[Fighting Style]] or [[Sword]], as the enemies are stunned by the shower of thunderbolts.

|{{Ability|C}}
* Large [[Area of Effect|AoE]].
* Pulls enemies upwards while stunning them.
* Great for countering air campers.
* Hitbox extends downwards, even if aimed upward.
* Great combo starter and follow-up.

|{{Ability|V}}
* Extremely large [[Area of Effect|AoE]], even after the recent nerfs.
* Extremely long range.
* Lands on [[Beast]] fruits even midair.
* Quick start-up. (Tap version)
* Fully held version deals insane damage.
* [[Instinct/Break|Breaks Instinct]].
* Quite easy to hit.
* Great combo starter/finisher.

|{{Ability|F}}
* Quick mobility.
* Very convenient for traversal.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Obsolete against [[Rubber]] users.
* Predictable.
* Not very good at aerial combat, as [X] and [V] often do not land/are extremely inconvenient to use.
* Passive 'charges' on the user's back heavily drop FPS, making them an overall nuisance during gameplay.
* All moves deal damage at separate parts, often making damage dealt low and inconsistent.
* Moves have bad endlag.

|{{Ability|TAP}}
* Almost useless in active PvP.
* Very low damage.
* Terrible range.

|{{Ability|Z}}
* Uses charges, making it very tedious to conserve charges for [F].
* Z1's damage is scaled lower when spammed.
* Z1 is largely useless, automatically needing Z2.
* Z3 takes time to charge, and is often outclassed by Z2.

|{{Ability|X}}
* Stun is escapable.
* Has a decent endlag, making it very punishable if missed.
* If the user is not wary, the move is very predictable.
* Hard to land midair, as the storm always forms directly in front of, and under the user.
* Extended version via Z1 is easy to avoid in active PvP.
* Extended beast via Z3 has extremely bad hitboxes and knockback, while also not working midair, making it largely useless.

|{{Ability|C}}
* Bad vertical range. 
* Very easy to [[Instinct]] trick.
* Endlag is punishable if missed.

|{{Ability|V}}
* Very long cooldown.
* Predictable, even more so when held.
* Although it ''can'' land midair, the angle the move is launched at is off center (due to its tendency to sink), making it nearly impossible to land consistently.
* High knockback.

|{{Ability|F}}
* No longer carries momentum.
* May not teleport if spammed too quickly.
* Held variation is useless, as the damage is extremely low, and just wastes a charge.
}}

|-|Notes=
{{Overview|Notes|
* Lightning's [X] move cannot be used in any place with a low roof, or any kind of cover. (Buildings, [[Magma Admiral]]'s volcano, etc)
** However, both [X] and [C] can still work normally if the roof is high enough (such as the roof of the [[Factory]]). 
* [X] Thunderstorm could be used in places with a roof before [[Updates/20|Update 20]], where it was changed to act like [C].
* After the rework, due to the new mechanics on [V] Thunderball Destruction, it too cannot be used under some places with roofs, as it will detonate instantly.
* Due to Lightning being easily countered in aerial combat (with the only reliable functional move being [C] Sky Judgement), it is recommended to use it as a supporting stun fruit for [[Swords]] and [[Guns]] instead.
* It is highly recommended to use [Z] Soul Shaker of the [[Skull Guitar]] after using [V] Thunderball Destruction, as it negates the knockback.
* The final panel upgrade, Conductor's Resonance, is extremely pricey, and requires the user to eat an additional physical Lightning, whilst already having Lightning activated, essentially wasting an entire fruit.
** Unless absolutely needed for completion purposes, it is highly recommended to ignore this upgrade outright, as the extended beast is nearly useless in both PvP and PvE, due to its terrible hitbox and awful damage, even being unable to hit enemies midair.
}}
</tabber>

